@startuml alert-sink-flow

title Alert Sink — Kafka Consume, Persist, Publish, Commit (CP5)

participant "Alert Evaluator" as AE
participant "Kafka\n(alerts topic)" as Kafka
participant "API Consumer\n(group: api)" as API
database "TimescaleDB\n(alerts)" as DB
database "Redis\n(alert-events)" as Redis

== Alert produced ==

AE -> Kafka : PRODUCE alerts\n{ alert_id, entity_id, alert_type,\n  status: NEW, payload, detected_at_ms }

== Alert consumed (eachMessage) ==

API -> Kafka : poll (group: api)
Kafka --> API : message at offset N

API -> API : parse + validate JSON payload

API -> DB : INSERT INTO alerts\n(...)\nON CONFLICT (alert_id) DO NOTHING
DB --> API : INSERT 1 0 (new row)\nor INSERT 0 0 (duplicate — safe)

API -> Redis : PUBLISH alert-events\n<alert JSON>
Redis --> API : 1 (subscriber count)

API -> Kafka : commitOffsets(offset N+1)

note over API, Kafka
  Commit is last. A crash before this point
  causes Kafka to redeliver. The idempotent
  INSERT absorbs the duplicate DB write.
  Redis publish may repeat — clients deduplicate
  by alert_id.
end note

== Dashboard hydration — GET /alerts ==

participant Browser

Browser -> API : GET /alerts\nCookie: sentinel_jwt=...
API -> API : requireAuth: verify JWT
API -> DB : SELECT * FROM alerts\nWHERE status IN ('NEW','ACKNOWLEDGED')\nORDER BY detected_at DESC
DB --> API : alert rows
API --> Browser : 200 [ alert rows ]

@enduml
